\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Look, my dear son, my servant
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 will serve me in wisdom
\par will obey my commandments
\par and to do my wishes
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par to redeem my dear nation;
\par out-door himself in grace,
\par in truth and might, but will be
\par lifted and crucified.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. He is going to suffer
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 disfigured in the face
\par people will disgrace him too
\par and take him to be cursed
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But look that suffering will work
\par mysteriously for men
\par and ginger them with new strength
\par new love, new zeal and life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My servant came to the world
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 amongst all human beings
\par He'd not reveal his glory
\par he was n't so handsome
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He was despised and shunned
\par many did not like him,
\par They hid their faces from him
\par they made him miserable.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Why? what about this falsehood?
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 What ill-luck follows him?
\par which has made God Himself to
\par  extend His wrath on Him?
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Did he with strong argument
\par has so offended God?
\par and He with this punishment
\par repaying for His deeds?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Really, all, all, our ailments
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 He alone carried all
\par and all our distresses too
\par He solely bore them all
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Because of our transgressions
\par He was so cruelly whipped
\par He was severely punished
\par so we can have our peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. He was severely tortured
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 he bore it quietly
\par He was led just like a sheep
\par soberly to be killed
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par As a lamb so dumbfounded
\par led before his sharers
\par likewise he was so quiet
\par and ne'er opened his mouth.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. His soul was swiftly taken
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj from among the living
\par and he'll be taken from His great agony.
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj He laid down his life freely
\par just as a sacrifice.
\par His decendants, He will see
\par and to gain eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Because the sins of many
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 He suffered and he died
\par Who ever believes in him
\par shall get eternal life
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par the worries of his spirit
\par won him more righteous men
\par And bring them to his father
\par as his beloved children.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. God will feed him to his fill
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj He will give him people
\par Great people and small people as  \tab    \tab 
\par reward of merit
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj Jesus, because of your love
\par we who are also here
\par add us up to your children
\par so we receive your life.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

